You can use a loop that continues to prompt the user until a valid input is received. Here's a sample method that does that:
public static int getChoice(List<String> options) {
    Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
    int choice;
    while (true) {
        // Display the options
        for (int i = 0; i < options.size(); i++) {
            System.out.println((i + 1) + ". " + options.get(i));
        }

        // Get user input
        System.out.print("Enter your choice: ");
        try {
            choice = Integer.parseInt(scanner.nextLine());
            if (choice >= 1 && choice <= options.size()) {
                return choice - 1; // Return 0-based index
            } else {
                System.out.println("Invalid choice. Please enter a number between 1 and " + options.size() + ".");
            }
        } catch (NumberFormatException e) {
            System.out.println("Invalid input. Please enter a number.");
        }
    }
}
